  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Monday)\nIssued at 905 PM CDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nThe start of the long term will offer more of the same as we \nremain under the influence of high pressure to our north. This \nwill bring another warm and dry day on Friday before the forecast \nbecomes much more troubled. \n\nAs we move into the weekend timeframe attention shifts to what is\ncurrently Invest 92L in the Gulf of America. Over the last 24 hour \nvarious ensemble and deterministic models have begun producing \nsolutions that spin Invest 92L into a tropical system and push it \nnorth towards the Gulf coast. When taking a deeper dive in the \nensembles, the key difference in the models appears to be the \nevolution of a shortwave passing through TX from Friday into \nSaturday. A faster progression of the short wave allows it to phase \nwell with Invest 92L and surges the system north. A slower solution \nkeeps the Invest 92L somewhat disorganized and with significantly \nless northward progression. Somewhat obviously, the first presented \nsolutions would be of greater concern to our local area. Nonetheless,\nit is much much too soon to look into any specifics should Invest \n92L take a northward path. Rather, we will be monitoring the track \nand timing of the shortwave to assess the probability of the two \nfeatures phasing. \n\nFor now, kept blended guidance that gradually bring Gulf moisture \ninto our area and increases rain chances through the weekend. This \nforecast still brings 1-2 inches of rain area wide so at minimum we \nare currently looking at a dreary weekend.",
